 35CL    31P(A,P),(A,N):RESONANCES     1964KU12,1971MC23,1975SC40ENSDF    202509
 35CL  H TYP=FUL$AUT=LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN$                                    
 35CL2 H CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2025$                                             
 35CL  H TYP=FUL$AUT=JUN CHEN, JOHN CAMERON AND BALRAJ SINGH$                   
 35CL2 H CIT=NDS 112,2715 (2011)$CUT=20-Oct-2011$                               
 35CL c  J|p=1/2+ {+31}P ground state.                                          
 35CL c  1975Sc40: {+31}P(|a,p) with 3.25-5.55-MeV |a beams produced from the   
 35CL2c  5.5-MV Van de Graaff accelerator of the University of Lowell. The      
 35CL3c  target was prepared by evaporating natural {+31}P onto carbon backings.
 35CL4c  Protons were detected using four silicon surface-barrier detectors.    
 35CL5c  Measured proton yields and angular distributions. Deduced resonance    
 35CL6c  levels at E{-x}=9.9-11.8 MeV, J, and |p.                               
 35CL d
 35CL c  1971Mc23: {+31}P(|a,p) with 3.25-5.25-MeV |a beams produced from the   
 35CL2c  5.5-MeV Van de Graaff accelerator of the Southern Universities Nuclear 
 35CL3c  Institute. The target was Zn{-3}P{-2} evaporated onto carbon backings. 
 35CL4c  Protons were detected using four solid state detectors. Measured proton
 35CL5c  yields and angular distributions. Deduced resonance levels at          
 35CL6c  E{-x}=9.9-11.7 MeV, J, and resonance strengths.                        
 35CL d
 35CL c  1964Ku12: {+31}P(|a,p) with 1.7-3.3-MeV |a beams produced from the     
 35CL2c  Utrecht Van de Graaff accelerator. A zinc phosphide target was prepared
 35CL3c  by evaporation of 40-500- mg/cm{+2} Zn{-3}P{-2} onto solid copper      
 35CL4c  backings. Protons were detected using five silicon surface barrier     
 35CL5c  counters at 87|', 120|', 135|', 150|', and 172|'. Measured resonance   
 35CL6c  yields and proton angular distributions. Deduced {+35}Cl resonance     
 35CL7c  energies, J, and resonance strengths.                                  
 35CL d
 35CL c  1970Um01: {+34}S(p,n), {+31}P(|a,n), {+31}P(|a,|a{-0}) reactions with  
 35CL2c  proton and |a beams produced from the Florida State University Tandem  
 35CL3c  Van de Graaff accelerator. Targets for {+34}S(p,n) were a CdS target by
 35CL4c  evaporating {+34}S enriched CdS onto 0.12-mm gold plate and a AgS      
 35CL5c  target heating {+34}S (67% enriched) in the presence of 0.025-mm Ag    
 35CL6c  foil. Targets for {+31}P(a,n) were prepared by evaporating natural     
 35CL7c  Ca{-3}P{-2} onto 0.075-mm Ta plate and 0.025-mm Al foil. Positrons from
 35CL8c  {+34}Cl decay were detected using an NE102 plastic scintillator. |g    
 35CL9c  rays in {+34}S following the decay were detected using a Ge(Li)        
 35CLAc  detector. Measured excitation functions. Deduced level energies and    
 35CLBc  isospin T=3/2 for {+35}Cl resonance states at 12.9 and 13.9 MeV.       
 35CL d
 35CL cL E$From E{-c.m.}+S(|a)({+35}Cl), where S(|a)({+35}Cl)=6997.91 {I4}      
 35CL2cL (2021Wa16). E{-c.m.}=E{-|a}(lab)|*m({+31}P)/[m{-|a}+m({+31}P)].        
 35CL cL J$Spin-parities are from analysis of measured angular distributions in 
 35CL2cL 1964Ku12, 1971Mc23, and 1975Sc40.                                      
 35CL cL J(K),S(K)$ From 1964Ku12, unless otherwise noted                       
 35CL cL J(M),S(M)$ From 1971Mc23, unless otherwise noted                       
 35CL cL J(S),S(S)$ From 1975Sc40, unless otherwise noted                       
 35CL cL E(U)$From 1970Um01. Two {+35}Cl resonances are found in {+34}S(p,n) and
 35CL2cL {+31}P(|a,n), but not in {+31}P(|a,|a{-0}) reactions. T=1 {+34}S g.s.  
 35CL3cL and T=1/2 protons can populate either T=1/2 or T=3/2 states in {+35}Cl.
 35CL4cL T=1/2 {+31}P g.s. and T=0 |a particles can populate T=1/2 states in    
 35CL5cL {+35}Cl. A small isospin impurity would allow formation of T=3/2 states
 35CL6cL in {+35}Cl. The lack of resonances in {+31}P(|a,|a{-0}) indicates that 
 35CL7cL these two resonances are most likely T=3/2. A T=3/2 resonances in      
 35CL8cL {+31}P(|a,|a{-0}) scattering is doubly isospin forbidden (both entrance
 35CL9cL and exit channels) compared with singly forbidden (entrance channel    
 35CLAcL only) for {+31}P(|a,n).                                                
 35CL cL S(E)$ Weighted average from 1964Ku12 and 1975Sc40                      
